      <!-- Question 6: Essay - Sample Size for Power -->
      <item ident="q6_essay" title="Question 6: Sample Size for Power">
        <itemmetadata>
          <qtimetadata>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>essay_question</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>3</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
          </qtimetadata>
        </itemmetadata>
        <presentation>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html"><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Sample Size for Power (3 points)</strong></p>
<p>A researcher is planning a study to test whether a new medication reduces systolic blood pressure. Based on pilot data, the population standard deviation is estimated to be σ = 20 mmHg. The researcher wants to detect a mean reduction of 10 mmHg from the population mean of 145 mmHg.</p>
<p>Using a significance level of α = 0.05 (two-sided) and desired power of 0.80, calculate the required sample size using R's <code>power.t.test()</code> function for a one-sample t-test.</p>
<p><strong>Provide your answer in the following format:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Your R code</li>
<li>The required sample size (rounded UP to the nearest whole number)</li>
<li>Brief interpretation (1-2 sentences)</li>
</ol>
            ]]></mattext>
          </material>
          <response_str ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
            <render_fib>
              <response_label ident="answer1" rshuffle="No"/>
            </render_fib>
          </response_str>
        </presentation>
        <resprocessing>
          <outcomes>
            <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
          </outcomes>
        </resprocessing>
      </item>

      <!-- Question 7A: Essay - ANOVA F-statistic -->
      <item ident="q7a_essay" title="Question 7A: ANOVA F-statistic">
        <itemmetadata>
          <qtimetadata>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>essay_question</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
            <qtimetadatafield>
              <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
              <fieldentry>1.5</fieldentry>
            </qtimetadatafield>
          </qtimetadata>
        </itemmetadata>
        <presentation>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html"><![CDATA[
<p><strong>ANOVA F-statistic (1.5 points)</strong></p>
<p>A researcher compares the effectiveness of three different exercise programs on weight loss (in kg) over 8 weeks. The data are:</p>
<table border="1" cellpadding="5">
<tr><th>Program A</th><th>Program B</th><th>Program C</th></tr>
<tr><td>4.2</td><td>6.1</td><td>7.8</td></tr>
<tr><td>3.8</td><td>5.8</td><td>8.2</td></tr>
<tr><td>4.5</td><td>6.4</td><td>7.5</td></tr>
<tr><td>4.1</td><td>5.9</td><td>8.0</td></tr>
<tr><td>4.3</td><td>6.2</td><td>7.9</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Perform a one-way ANOVA to test if there is a significant difference in mean weight loss across the three programs. Use α = 0.05.</p>
<p><strong>Provide your answer in the following format:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Your R code to create the data and perform ANOVA</li>
<li>The F-statistic (rounded to 2 decimal places)</li>
<li>The p-value</li>
<li>Your conclusion (1-2 sentences)</li>
</ol>
            ]]></mattext>
          </material>
          <response_str ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
            <render_fib>
              <response_label ident="answer1" rshuffle="No"/>
            </render_fib>
          </response_str>
        </presentation>
        <resprocessing>
          <outcomes>
            <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
          </outcomes>
        </resprocessing>
      </item>

      <!-- Question 7B: Essay - Two-Sample t-Test p-value -->
