            <mattext texttype="text/html"><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Test Statistic Calculation (3 points)</strong></p>
<p>A researcher compares mean test scores between two teaching methods. The summary statistics are:</p>
<ul>
<li>Method 1: n<sub>1</sub> = 20, mean = 85.3, s<sub>1</sub> = 12.4</li>
<li>Method 2: n<sub>2</sub> = 18, mean = 78.6, s<sub>2</sub> = 14.1</li>
</ul>
<p>Calculate the test statistic (t-value) for a two-sample t-test (assume equal variances) using the formula provided in class.</p>
<p><strong>Provide your answer in the following format:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Calculate pooled standard deviation (show work)</li>
<li>Calculate standard error (show work)</li>
<li>Calculate t-statistic (show work)</li>
<li>Final t-statistic value (rounded to 2 decimal places)</li>
</ol>
            ]]></mattext>
          </material>
          <response_str ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
