        </itemmetadata>
        <presentation>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html"><![CDATA[
<p><strong>Power Calculation (3 points)</strong></p>
<p>A researcher is planning a one-sample study to test whether a new intervention changes blood glucose levels. Based on prior research:</p>
<ul>
<li>Expected sample size: n = 30</li>
<li>Expected mean difference to detect: δ = 12 mg/dL</li>
<li>Population standard deviation: σ = 18 mg/dL</li>
<li>Significance level: α = 0.05 (two-sided)</li>
</ul>
<p>Calculate the statistical power of this study using R's <code>power.t.test()</code> function.</p>
<p><strong>Provide your answer in the following format:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Your R code</li>
<li>The power value (rounded to 2 decimal places, as a proportion not percentage)</li>
<li>Interpret the power in context (2-3 sentences)</li>
</ol>
            ]]></mattext>
          </material>
          <response_str ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
